According to Eq. (\ref{Deff_PX_as_MUBS}), the coordinate and momentum eigenvectors form mutually unbiased bases, which means that if a system is prepared in a state from one of the bases, then all outcomes of the measurement with respect to the other basis are equally probable.

The finite-dimensional Schr\"{o}dinger equation is
